        "# Hotel Search Ranking, Part 2: Features and Baselines\n",
        "\n",
        "Part 1 left me with a to do list: clean the prices, stop trusting raw clicks, compare prices within each search, and keep `position` out of the model. This notebook works through that list and then asks a simple question before any machine learning happens:\n",
        "\n",
        "**How good are the obvious ways of sorting hotels?** Cheapest first, best reviewed first, most popular first, and Expedia's own order. Those scores are the bar the real model in Part 3 has to clear. A fancy model that can't beat \"sort by review score\" isn't worth anything.\n",
        "\n",
        "Author: Siddharth Suman"
      ]
    },
