      "source": [
        "## Cleaning\n",
        "\n",
        "Three fixes from Part 1:\n",
        "\n",
        "* Prices above $10,000 or at zero aren't real room prices, so I blank them out rather than delete the rows. Deleting rows would remove hotels from a search list, and then the list wouldn't be what the guest actually saw.\n",
        "* A star rating or review score of 0 means \"not rated\", so it becomes missing.\n",
        "* A historical price of 0 means the hotel wasn't sold in that period, so that becomes missing too.\n",
        "\n",
        "Then the label the model learns from, using the competition's scoring: **5 for a booking, 1 for a click, 0 for nothing.**"
      ]
    },
