      "source": [
        "## Splitting by time, not at random\n",
        "\n",
        "In real life a ranking model is trained on the past and used on the future. So I split searches by date instead of at random:\n",
        "\n",
        "* **History** (oldest 40% of searches): used only to work out how popular each hotel is. The model never trains or gets scored on these.\n",
        "* **Train** (next 40%): what the model learns from in Part 3.\n",
        "* **Test** (newest 20%): kept aside for the final score.\n",
        "\n",
        "Keeping a separate history period matters for the popularity feature. If a hotel's popularity were worked out from the same searches the model is scored on, the model would partly be looking at the answer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "id": "e0cea22f",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "e0cea22f",
        "outputId": "944a8c9e-620b-4f7b-88ec-ae1f2ab474c5"
      },
