      },
      "source": [
        "## Hotel popularity, measured fairly\n",
        "\n",
        "Part 1 showed that clicks are heavily shaped by position: a hotel Expedia often put at the top collects clicks partly for that reason. So I build two popularity measures from the **history period only**:\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Booking rate**: bookings divided by the number of times the hotel was shown. Bookings are a much stronger signal than clicks.\n",
        "* **Click rate in random searches**: clicks from searches where the order was shuffled, so every hotel had the same chance of being seen.\n",
        "\n",
        "Many hotels were only shown a handful of times, and one lucky booking would make them look amazing. To avoid that, each rate is pulled towards the overall average until the hotel has been shown about 20 times. Hotels that never appeared in the history period simply get the average."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "id": "74497884",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "74497884",
        "outputId": "2521887e-fe82-47fd-c1a4-060e7bb76101"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Test rows where the hotel already appeared in the history period: 95%\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "hist = df[df['period'] == 'history']\n",
        "SMOOTH = 20\n",
        "\n",
        "avg_booking = hist['booking_bool'].mean()\n",
        "pop = hist.groupby('prop_id').agg(shown=('booking_bool', 'size'), booked=('booking_bool', 'sum'))\n",
        "pop['hotel_booking_rate'] = (pop['booked'] + SMOOTH * avg_booking) / (pop['shown'] + SMOOTH)\n",
        "\n",
        "hist_rnd = hist[hist['random_bool'] == 1]\n",
        "avg_click_rnd = hist_rnd['click_bool'].mean()\n",
        "pop_rnd = hist_rnd.groupby('prop_id').agg(shown=('click_bool', 'size'), clicked=('click_bool', 'sum'))\n",
        "pop_rnd['hotel_click_rate_random'] = (pop_rnd['clicked'] + SMOOTH * avg_click_rnd) / (pop_rnd['shown'] + SMOOTH)\n",
        "\n",
        "df = df.merge(pop[['hotel_booking_rate']], left_on='prop_id', right_index=True, how='left')\n",
        "df = df.merge(pop_rnd[['hotel_click_rate_random']], left_on='prop_id', right_index=True, how='left')\n",
        "df['hotel_seen_before'] = df['hotel_booking_rate'].notna().astype(int)\n",
        "df['hotel_booking_rate'] = df['hotel_booking_rate'].fillna(avg_booking)\n",
        "df['hotel_click_rate_random'] = df['hotel_click_rate_random'].fillna(avg_click_rnd)\n",
        "\n",
        "test_rows = df[df['period'] == 'test']\n",
        "print(f\"Test rows where the hotel already appeared in the history period: {test_rows['hotel_seen_before'].mean():.0%}\")"
      ]
    },
