      "metadata": {
        "id": "73683a7e"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Scoring a ranking: NDCG\n",
        "\n",
        "For each search I sort the hotels by some score and check where the booked and clicked hotels ended up. NDCG gives full marks when the booked hotel is first and the clicked ones come right after, and fewer points the further down they land. I use the usual formula, where a booking (5) is worth far more than a click (1), and report it for the top 5 (what a guest sees without scrolling) and the top 38 (the whole list, as in the original competition).\n",
        "\n",
        "Searches with no click and no booking can't be scored, because there's nothing to find, so they're left out. When two hotels have exactly the same score, I break the tie at random so no baseline gets lucky from the original order."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "id": "dbd31f98",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "dbd31f98",
        "outputId": "97ca8035-7b93-48c4-fb4c-3604129773ca"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Perfect order: 1.0 | Worst order: 0.51\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def ndcg(frame, score_col, k, seed=0):\n",
        "    d = frame[['srch_id', 'relevance', score_col]].copy()\n",
        "    d['tiebreak'] = np.random.default_rng(seed).random(len(d))\n",
        "    d = d.sort_values(['srch_id', score_col, 'tiebreak'], ascending=[True, False, True])\n",
        "    rank = d.groupby('srch_id').cumcount() + 1\n",
        "    dcg = np.where(rank <= k, (2.0 ** d['relevance'] - 1) / np.log2(rank + 1), 0)\n",
        "    dcg = pd.Series(dcg, index=d.index).groupby(d['srch_id']).sum()\n",
        "\n",
        "    ideal = d.sort_values(['srch_id', 'relevance'], ascending=[True, False])\n",
        "    irank = ideal.groupby('srch_id').cumcount() + 1\n",
        "    idcg = np.where(irank <= k, (2.0 ** ideal['relevance'] - 1) / np.log2(irank + 1), 0)\n",
        "    idcg = pd.Series(idcg, index=ideal.index).groupby(ideal['srch_id']).sum()\n",
        "\n",
        "    scored = idcg > 0\n",
        "    return (dcg[scored] / idcg[scored]).mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Quick sanity check on a made up search: perfect order should score 1, worst order much lower\n",
        "toy = pd.DataFrame({'srch_id': [1, 1, 1], 'relevance': [5, 1, 0],\n",
        "                    'good': [3, 2, 1], 'bad': [1, 2, 3]})\n",
        "print(\"Perfect order:\", round(ndcg(toy, 'good', 5), 3), \"| Worst order:\", round(ndcg(toy, 'bad', 5), 3))"
      ]
    },
