        "### What this tells me\n",
        "\n",
        "This is the pattern I wanted to check before trusting any model. If cheap hotels win a lot of clicks but turn fewer of those clicks into bookings, then a model trained mostly on clicks would push cheap rooms too high. Guests would be tempted by the price, look, and then leave without booking. A hotelier would recognise this straight away: a low rate gets attention, but the room still has to look worth it once the guest opens the page.\n",
        "\n",
        "This is one more reason the model in Part 3 will learn from the 5, 1, 0 scale, where a booking counts five times as much as a click, and why Part 4 will check whether the final model leans too hard on price."
      ]
